# All optional. Addresses, chain, scan floor and RPC endpoints come from
# @cobuilders/safenet-core, which configures Mainnet only.

# Where these go: Vite reads env from the repository root, not from apps/web. For `pnpm dev`
# and `pnpm build` it loads the root .env and .env.local, the file `pnpm env:pull` writes and
# overwrites. Copy what you need from here into the root .env.

# Optional - RPC endpoints, tried in this order.
#
# NEVER PUT A KEY HERE. Vite writes every VITE_ value into the file this app ships to
# IPFS. That file is public and permanent. A provider API key in these variables
# is a key you have given away. Keep private endpoints in .env.local at the repository
# root, under a name without the VITE_ prefix. Vite reads that file too, but puts only
# VITE_ values into the bundle, and `pnpm check:browser` fails if a value from it longer than
# 12 characters turns up there. It does not see shorter values.
#
# Setting any one of these REPLACES the built-in list. It does not extend it.
#
# VITE_RPC_URL=
# VITE_RPC_URL_FALLBACK_1=
# VITE_RPC_URL_FALLBACK_2=

# Optional - subgraph query URLs for the Network Overview, one per chain.
#
# THESE ARE PUBLIC. The browser sends every query to this URL, so anyone who opens the page can
# read it in the network panel and in the bundle. Use a URL that needs no key. Never put a Graph
# gateway URL with an API key in its path here: that is a key you have given away. Serve such an
# endpoint through a proxy that adds the key, and put the proxy's URL here.
#
# Unset, in development and in a production build alike, the app queries the Subgraph Studio
# deployment of each chain: the default in packages/core/src/subgraphs.ts. That is Studio's
# development URL, rate-limited to about 3,000 queries a day per subgraph, and not the
# production read path. To read the local graph-node from `pnpm graph:up` instead, set each
# variable to its URL there: http://127.0.0.1:<GRAPH_NODE_PORT>/subgraphs/name/safenet/<chain>,
# with the port from .env.ports and the chain mainnet or gnosis.
#
# VITE_SUBGRAPH_URL_MAINNET=
# VITE_SUBGRAPH_URL_GNOSIS=

# Optional — wallet connection
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional — Merkle drop rewards contract address
VITE_MERKLE_DROP_ADDRESS=

# Optional — compliance
VITE_SANCTIONS_API_URL=
VITE_GEOBLOCK_CACHE_DAYS=

# Optional — validator info endpoint (defaults to SEF's published file, SEF_DATA in packages/core)
VITE_VALIDATOR_INFO_URL=

# Optional — rewards base URL. Replaces every source when set. Unset, the app reads SEF's IPFS
# dataset behind rewards.safenet-gov.eth, then the repository (src/rewards-source.ts in packages/core)
VITE_REWARDS_BASE_URL=

# Optional — an IPFS gateway tried before the public ones for SEF's reward dataset
VITE_IPFS_GATEWAY=

# Optional — analytics (Plausible); set to your site domain to enable tracking
VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=

# Optional — canonical app URL for social preview meta tags (og:image, twitter:image); absolute URLs are required for social crawlers
VITE_APP_URL=

# Optional — footer links
VITE_DOCS_URL=
VITE_TERMS_URL=
VITE_PRIVACY_URL=
VITE_IMPRINT_URL=
